## Install and run

Requires Python 3.11+.

Windows (PowerShell):
```powershell
py -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt
copy .env.example .env     # optional: add keys
streamlit run app.py
```
macOS / Linux:
```bash
python3 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env
streamlit run app.py
```
Run the tests: `python -m pytest -q`

## Environment variables (.env, never committed)

- `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID`: create a bot with @BotFather, message it, then read your chat id from
  `https://api.telegram.org/bot<token>/getUpdates`. Settings page has a test-message button.
- `SEC_USER_AGENT="Your Name you@email.com"`: required by SEC for filings/financials. Without it those parts are
  switched off (the app says so); nothing is guessed.
- `ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY`: optional, technical-analysis page only (free tier is rate-limited).

## How the scanner decides

Pre-filters (editable): price 2-50 USD, average dollar volume >= 5M (mean of earlier sessions), spread <= 0.5% only when
a real bid/ask exists, at least 3 earlier sessions for baselines.

Features (1-minute completed bars, regular session): RVOL of the last 5 minutes versus the same window in earlier sessions
(smoothed +-5 min; cumulative RVOL is shown for information), VWAP, 1/5/15-minute returns and acceleration, break of the
15-minute high, hold ratio after the break, EMA20/EMA50, RSI, 15-minute strength versus SPY.

Score = 100 x sum(points)/sum(all weights). Default weights: RVOL 25, momentum 20, breakout 20, liquidity 15, relative
strength 10, continuation 10. A component with missing data scores 0 but keeps its weight, so **missing data can only
lower a score**; `coverage` shows how much of the score is backed by data and candidates below 60% are never actionable.
The score is a ranking aid. **It is not a probability of success.**

States: watching, early indicators, approaching breakout, confirmed breakout (RVOL, 5-min return and score thresholds),
failed (closed back below the level), expired (30 min without renewal). "Extended" moves (far above the level/VWAP) are
flagged and not actionable. Market closed or stale data also makes everything non-actionable.

Alerts fire on new events only: first alert, a higher-ranked state, a failure after a confirmed alert, a new higher
level, or a score jump of 15+. A repeat of the same state needs a reset and the cooldown.

## Backtest rules (scanner)

Signal on a completed bar, fill at the next bar's open plus assumed slippage and commission; if target and stop fall in the
same 1-minute bar the result is "ambiguous" and counts as not a win; stop gaps fill at the open; sessions are split
chronologically into development and hold-out; random-entry and simple-momentum baselines use the same costs and universe;
rates come with Wilson 95% intervals and a "too few samples" flag. Nothing is tuned by the code.

## Calibration

A probability is shown only if: >= 200 resolved signals, >= 4 sessions, enough wins and losses in both parts, a positive
score slope, and a Brier-score gain of >= 2% over a constant base rate on **later sessions**, confirmed in >= 95% of
bootstrap resamples. Otherwise the page says why none is shown.

## Company history: how causes are labelled

Events are detected on split-adjusted daily closes with configurable thresholds and compared with SPY. Splits are never
reported as crashes. Each event gets one label: **direct evidence** (a high-weight SEC filing was accepted before the first
move day's open and the move is abnormal and not market-driven), **probable** (two clues or unclear timing),
**coincident**, or **unresolved**. The tool matches filing type and timing only; **it does not read the filing text**, and
free sources have no historical news archive, so no news is attributed to old events.

## Data provider limitations (read this)

- yfinance is unofficial, delayed and rate-limited. 1-minute history is about 7 days; 5/15-minute about 60 days; 1-hour about
  730 days. It has no bid/ask, so spread is "unavailable" and costs in backtests are assumptions.
- There is **no real-time feed and no WebSocket vendor wired in**. `scanner/stream.py` is a tested reconnect/de-dup wrapper for
  one to be added later (a paid provider such as Polygon, Alpaca or Finnhub). Until then every price is labelled delayed.
- The Nasdaq Trader list contains currently listed names only (survivorship bias for any historical study).
- yfinance `Close` is split-adjusted, `AdjClose` also dividend-adjusted; raw as-traded prices are not available.
- Holiday/early-close calendar is rule-based; one-off closures (national mourning days, weather) are not known.
- PDF export: open the HTML report in a browser and print to PDF.

